<title>USA: Norfolk plans increase in cap improvements.</title>
<headline>Norfolk plans increase in cap improvements.</headline>
<dateline>NORFOLK, Va. 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norfolk Southern Corp said Thursday it plans to spend $792 million on capital improvements in 1997.</p>
<p>The company said this compares with $708 million planned for 1996.</p>
<p>The company said its projected 1997 capital spending includes more than $100 million for equipment and facilities for an automotive mixing center network it is developing under a 12-year contract with Ford Motor Co.</p>
<p>Excluding this project, the company said its capital spending is actually less than that budgeted for 1996.</p>
</text>
